{
  "id": 491595389,
  "iid": 25213,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "nts-ke: have a direction variable with request/response/unknown values.",
  "description": "This makes the code in dissect_nts_ke() a little clearer, as you don't\nhave separate \"do I know the direction\" and \"is it a request or\nresponse\" variables.\n\nIt also works better with compilers such as the GCC 10.5 in NetBSD 10\nthat don't get the dataflow analysis right and don't realize that, in\nsome places, it's known that the old \"request\" variable was set because\nthe \"direction_determined\" variable is true, and thus issue a bogus \"may\nbe used uninitialized\" warning.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
